Subject: [202505] Skip the unused Buster build environment by default

The selected docker-sonic-vs.gz, sonic-vs.img.gz and sonic-broadcom.bin
targets do not require Buster runtime layers. The VS PTF images still use
Buster, but are separate test-image targets, not part of these outputs.
Upstream configure nevertheless initializes every enabled build environment;
its default NOBUSTER=0 fails on the retired Buster security mirror.

Use the upstream NOBUSTER switch instead of changing mirrors or removing
image dependencies. Keep Bullseye and Bookworm enabled. An explicit
NOBUSTER=0 still permits callers to request the old environment.

Failure: https://github.com/ITJamie/sonic-vs-builder/actions/runs/42684597504
Upstream source: https://github.com/sonic-net/sonic-buildimage/blob/ff3c0c9f686a1d0dbddbe813b233b3b7a51bd8e2/Makefile
Verified against ff3c0c9f686a1d0dbddbe813b233b3b7a51bd8e2.
Remove once upstream defaults NOBUSTER to 1. Reassess if selected image
dependencies start requiring Buster; this does not port optional PTF images.

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 
 NOJESSIE ?= 1
 NOSTRETCH ?= 1
-NOBUSTER ?= 0
+NOBUSTER ?= 1
 NOBULLSEYE ?= 0
 NOBOOKWORM ?= 0
 
